Mapping & Driver Verification Strategy

Mapping & Driver Verification Strategy

Date: August 11, 2026

Current Decision

SCUBER is being developed with a free/low-cost-first strategy while the app is still in development and testing.

Mapping Strategy

Do not set up Google Maps Platform or Google Cloud billing yet.

For the development/testing version of SCUBER:

Use Leaflet as the open-source map interface.
Use OpenStreetMap-based map data for development/testing.
Do not add Google Maps API keys or Google billing at this stage.
Do not add paid routing/navigation services yet.
Map Development Order

Build the mapping system in layers:

Interactive map
Replace the current Live Trip Map placeholder with an actual map.
Pickup and destination
Display the rider's pickup location.
Display the destination.
Driver GPS
Have the driver's device provide the driver's current location.
Live rider tracking
Send the driver's location through SCUBER's backend.
Display the driver's moving vehicle marker on the rider's map.
Routing/navigation
Add routing/navigation only after the basic live-location system works and SCUBER actually needs it.
Important Cost Constraint

SCUBER should avoid unnecessary paid services during development.

Do not activate or pay for mapping, routing, navigation, or verification services until the specific feature requires them.

OpenStreetMap's public tile servers should be treated as a development/testing option, not assumed to be the permanent production map infrastructure for a commercial rideshare application.

Driver Verification Strategy

Driver document verification will eventually be handled through a specialized third-party verification service, rather than building document verification ourselves.

Potential future verification workflow:

Driver Application
→ Identity/document verification
→ Driver's license verification
→ Insurance/document verification
→ Other legally required screening
→ Approved Driver

The verification provider has not been selected yet.

Do not activate a verification service yet. First establish SCUBER's actual driver onboarding and compliance requirements.

