SCUBER Phase 2: Road Routing

I would build it in this order:

1. Road-based route 🛣️
Draw an actual route along roads between pickup and destination instead of a straight line/bounds-only map.

2. Driver's route 🚗
The driver sees the route from their current location toward the pickup, then toward the destination.

3. Rider sees progress
The rider sees the driver's moving vehicle on the road route.

4. Re-routing
If the driver moves significantly off the planned route, SCUBER can eventually request a new route.

5. ETA
Once we have actual road distance and travel time, we can make the ETA much more meaningful.

And I would still keep our cost strategy

I wouldn't jump straight to Google Maps.

We can investigate an open-source/low-cost routing service that works with the Leaflet map we're already using. That lets us prove the routing architecture before committing SCUBER to a paid mapping platform.

So our architecture becomes:

Leaflet
↓
OpenStreetMap map data
↓
Routing engine
↓
Road route
↓
Driver GPS
↓
Moving driver marker
↓
Rider sees live trip

And today's checkpoint gives us a very important foundation:

GPS + Firestore + live rider map are already proven.

I would call the next checkpoint SCUBER Phase 2 — Road Routing & Navigation, rather than replacing the map we've built. We're adding the road intelligence to it.
